{"name":"Quitting smoking / vaping","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/61464d51-e557-4c2f-9198-f21a3de122ca/thumb/","credit":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/127173209@N05/16272143521","caption":"E-Cigarette/Electronic Cigarette/E-Cigs/E-Liquid/Vaping/Stop Smoking/Quit Smoking","source":"Flickr"},"mentions":13,"casual":{"lead":["Smokers tend to show a characteristic aged look called smoker's face, with a distinctive wrinkle pattern and sallow grey skin. Some people quit to slow premature aging and look younger.","Smoking raises collagen- and elastin-degrading enzymes, narrows blood vessels and increases oxidative stress. A 1985 BMJ study reported certain facial features in about 46% of continuing smokers and 8% of former smokers who had smoked for a decade, and observational data show the features are less common in former smokers. How much reverses after quitting is not well established, and the sources reviewed do not address vaping and skin."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People quit by going cold turkey, tapering, or using nicotine replacement and cessation programmes, and track their skin tone and wrinkles over months. Medical support is available for those who need it."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Smoking carries major documented harms including cancers, heart and lung disease, and quitting is associated with falling lung cancer risk over years. Nicotine withdrawal causes irritability and cravings for a period."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/61464d51-e557-4c2f-9198-f21a3de122ca/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/7492/16272143521_1421022fef_b.jpg","title":"E-Cigarette/Electronic Cigarette/E-Cigs/E-Liquid/Vaping/Stop Smoking/Quit Smoking","license":"BY 2.0","creator":"Vaping360","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/127173209@N05/16272143521","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/581dd094-a3ac-4cb2-b41a-09cb8dff8c38/thumb/